# NG-BRDF-SPHERES: the GGX lobe across roughness, on one row of metals and one of dielectrics (roughness 0..1, step 0.1),
# plus a ClearCoat and a Cloth sphere; then a white furnace (uniform sky, F0 = 1 metals) - NG-BRDF pass 1/2:
# exact height-correlated Smith (Mesh/BRDF.glslh VisibilitySmith), the split-sum LUT and the multiple-scattering albedo table
# integrating the same Vis, and (pass 2) the anisotropic slab lobe compensated from the same table.
# Scene = Starter (Projects/Desert/Content/Scenes/Starter.desce, not saved): its 6-step rows stay at z -460/-300; the
# scenario spawns the 0.1-step rows at z 900 from Meshes/Modeling/Sphere.stmesh (bounds +-50 cm, so radius 50 cm).
# Materials (committed assets): M_Metal_R0..R100 / M_Dielectric_R0..R100 (the R10/30/50/70/90 ones added by NG-BRDF),
# M_Furnace_R0..R100 (StandardSurface, albedo 1, metallic 1: F0 = 1), M_BRDF_ClearCoat (ClearCoatSurface: red
# dielectric base roughness 0.6 under a coat of roughness 0.05), M_BRDF_Cloth (ClothSurface: dark blue, fuzz 0.8, Cloth 1).
# Entity UUIDs: metal i = 73100000000000001(00+i), dielectric i = ..2(00+i), clearcoat ..301, cloth ..302.
