# Key light as SSS-PROFILE (Starter is unitless: sun 1 lux at EV100 0.53 leaves the sun term invisible). A DirectionLight
# travels along its TRANSLATION (Scene.cpp:815): 30,-60,-100 = from behind the camera, up and to its left, so every
# sphere carries its sun highlight toward the camera.
Дано set 13376537502658031226 DirectionalLightData.Intensity 1000
Дано set 17921165617746467452 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.ManualExposureEV100 8.5
Дано run Entity Sun
Дано --subject selection set Translation 30,-60,-100
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,115,2000
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,0,-1
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.FOV 75
Когда --subject viewport drag 600,40 600,40 16
Тогда-вид brdf_spheres top row metals R0..R100 left to right, bottom row red dielectrics R0..R100, clearcoat far left, cloth far right. Metal row: the highlight widens and dims smoothly, the sphere's overall brightness does NOT fall toward R100 (multiple scattering keeps rough metal's energy), no brightness step between neighbours (no R0->R10 or R40->R50 jump). Dielectric row: same smooth widening, the red body colour constant. ClearCoat: a second sharp small highlight on top of the broad red one. Cloth: a soft bright sheen rim at grazing angles, no sharp highlight. editor.log 0 VUID
# --- white furnace: a uniform sky of radiance 0.5 in every direction (zenith = horizon = ground = night colour, no sun
# disc / glow / stars), every light off, the ground taken away so the lower hemisphere sees the sky too. A metal of F0 = 1
# reflects all of it at every roughness: the sphere reads the sky's brightness (Kulla-Conty / UE EnvBRDF energy terms).
