Тогда-вид brdf_furnace the top row (F0 = 1 metals R0..R100) reads uniformly at the sky's brightness: every sphere's mean within a few % of the sky behind it and of its neighbours, R100 not darker than R0, no dark rim at grazing angles beyond the edge's own anti-aliasing. (Rows below are not part of the check.) If every sphere still mirrors the old blue sky, the sky cube was not rebaked - that is a finding (AutoRebakeEnvironment), not a BRDF result.
